      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\), let's analyze the given information and use properties of angles and triangles.\n\n1. **Identify Given Angles and Triangle Properties:**\n   - \\(\\angle ABD = 93^\\circ\\)\n   - \\(\\angle CBD = 130^\\circ\\)\n   - \\(\\angle BCD = 180^\\circ\\) (as they form a straight line).\n\n2. **Calculate Arc Lengths:**\n   The measures of the arcs \\(BD\\) and \\(BC\\) can be determined using the following steps:\n   - Since \\(\\angle ABD = 93^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle CBD = 130^\\circ\\), the angle between \\(BD\\) and \\(BA\\) is \\(93^\\circ\\).\n   - The angle \\(\\angle BCD = 180^\\circ\\) implies that arc \\(BC\\) is 180 degrees (a completed circle).\n\n3. **Determine Arc Length \\(CD\\):**\n   The arc \\(CD\\) can be found by subtracting the given arcs:\n   \\[\n   \\angle ACB = \\angle BCD - \\text{arc length of } BC = 180^\\circ - 130^\\circ = 50^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\) is \\(\\boxed{50}\\) degrees.",
